cularly good, with the weather typically sunny and mild. The island is usually counted as one of the Dodecanese, but due to its importance for travelers is considered separately here. The rock-rose is so prolific here that it has been named the 'Island of Roses,' though modern scholars doubt the ancient theory that the island's name comes from the Greek word for rose.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Rhodes","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Rhodes","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Rhodes is a large Greek island where a walled medieval city meets the beaches. The Medieval City of Rhodes and the Palace of the Grand Master lead, with Kameiros further out. Its sights take about four hours, and April to June is the best stretch.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":12717,"visit_h":4.1}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-colossus-of-rhodes","name":"Colossus of Rhodes","kind":"Monument","lat":36.45111,"lon":28.22778,"dist_km":8.5,"rank_score":11.5,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Colosse_de_Rhodes_%28Barclay%29.jpg/960px-Colosse_de_Rhodes_%28Barclay%29.jpg","author":"gravure sur bois de Sidney Barclay numérisée Google","licence":"Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colosse_de_Rhodes_(Barclay).jpg","w":1170,"h":1600,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-palace-of-the-grand-master-of-the-knights-of-rhodes","name":"Palace of the Grand Master of the Knights of Rhodes","kind":"Museum","lat":36.44569,"lon":28.22411,"dist_km":7.9,"rank_score":8.07,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Palace_of_the_Grand_Master_of_the_Knights_of_Rhodes_%289451928431%29.jpg/960px-Palace_of_the_Grand_Master_of_the_Knights_of_Rhodes_%289451928431%29.jpg","author":"Jorge Láscar from Australia","licence":"CC BY 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palace_of_the_Gra